    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1179">

                <pb facs="0968" n="958" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg958"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.633/5–2649: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-05-26T13:00:00-04:00">May 26, 1949—1 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>640. From Butterworth.<anchor n="60" xml:id="d1179-f1"/> We are all very
                    disturbed by protracted confinement Ward and other members staff Mukden and wish
                    no stone left unturned to effect their speedy departure. I hope you will find
                    means personally to press this matter to a rapid conclusion. [Butterworth.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Webb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1179-f1" n="60" xml:id="d1179-f1-content">
                <p>W. Walton Butterworth, Director of the Office of Far Eastern Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
